"""Deli Counter 0.253.0 (the factory's roadmap 292): the enemy's body is the NPC's, and the NPC's is the
player's until it says otherwise.

The contract said the enemy's eye twice with nothing to say which governed. The bodies decide now: `npc_body()` is
`npc_standard`'s stated metrics over the player's, `sight_heights()` reads both eyes from the bodies and checks the
`sightlines` copies, `npc_standard` restates nothing, and no sightline copy is merged into a contract that omits it.
Lot 0.126.1 ships first.

What this writes, every target pinned by its hash and refused on a mismatch, nothing written until every file has been
worked out: `agent_contract.json`, `agent_contract.py` and `test_cover_breaks_sightlines.py` (anchored hunks); the new
`test_npc_body.py`; VERSION; the CHANGELOG entry, prepended. Generated from a proven clone
(`patches/dc_npc_body/gen_dc_npc_body.py`), dry-run on a fresh clone to the clone's every byte, a second run refused
(`patches/dc_npc_body/dry_run_*.out.txt`).

    python patches/patch_dc_npc_body.py
    cd deli_counter && python build.py --all && python -m pytest -q && python check.py
"""
