CHANGELOG = '## [0.253.0] - the enemy\'s body is the NPC\'s, and the NPC\'s is the player\'s until it says otherwise\n\n**The factory\'s roadmap 292.** `agent_contract.json` said the enemy\'s eye twice -- `characters.npc_standard`, whose\nNPCs "share player metrics until a distinct class ships", and `sightlines.enemy_sight_height_m` -- with nothing to say\nwhich governed, and the NPC block restated the player\'s radius and height, which nothing read. Level Factory\'s seam\nwrote the player\'s body into every Laser Tag run and left the enemy\'s eye at Laser Tag\'s 1.6; Level Factory 0.231.0\nreads this block for it.\n\n### Changed\n- **The bodies decide the sight heights.** `npc_body()` (new) is `npc_standard`\'s stated metrics over the player\'s.\n  `sight_heights()` (new) gives the two eyes -- the player\'s and the NPC body\'s -- and checks the `sightlines` copies\n  against them, refusing one that disagrees ("one body, one eye"), as `cover_break_height` already refused an aim\n  copy. `cover_break_height()` and `shelter_height()` ask it.\n- **`npc_standard` states no metric of its own.** Its restated radius and height are gone; its `shares_note` says what\n  governs and why, and `sightlines.sight_heights_are` that the copies are the bodies\'.\n- **No copy of a body-derived sightline number is merged into a contract that omits it.** `_DEFAULTS["sightlines"]` is\n  empty. A contract stating only its body -- a 2.05 m player with its chest at 1.15 m and no `sightlines` block -- was\n  refused, "one body, one aim point", for disagreeing with the 1.0 m aim copy the module had merged in;\n  `cover_break_height_m` was already kept out for that reason. `_player()` fills a partial player block field by field\n  from its ratified fallback, for the eyes.\n\n### Measured, kept\n- **Lot 0.126.1 ships first.** Lot\'s contract fallback mirrored the NPC\'s two numbers, and Lot 0.126.0\'s guard, run\n  against this contract, counts 19 shared keys against its floor of 21 and fails (the factory\'s\n  `patches/lot_npc_fallback/suite_clone_vs_base.out.txt`).\n- **The shells are rebuilt; no number of a body or a clearance moves.** `build_freshness.py` watches\n  `agent_contract.py` and `agent_contract.json`, so the library is rebuilt. The shipped contract\'s change is the NPC\n  block\'s two restated numbers and two notes; the player, the bake, the clearances and the sightline copies stand as\n  they were, and at them `sight_heights()` is (1.6, 1.6) and the crossing 1.3 m.\n\n### Tests\n- **test_npc_body.py** (new, 4): a studio states its body once and the crossing follows it -- 1.5 m for a 2.05 m body,\n  shelter at 1.85 m; the NPC is the player until it says otherwise; a sight height that disagrees with its body is\n  refused; the shipped NPC states no metric of its own. On 0.252.0 the first fails on behaviour ("one body, one aim\n  point") and so does the last (the restated radius and height); the other two fail on the new names (the factory\'s\n  `patches/dc_npc_body/prove_tests_on_0252.out.txt`).\n- **test_cover_breaks_sightlines.py**: the four fixtures that stated sight heights without the body that has them\n  state it now -- the eye, and for an enemy that differs, `npc_standard`\'s. On 0.252.0 the file passes.\n\n'
OLD_VERSION, NEW_VERSION = 'Deli Counter 0.252.0', 'Deli Counter 0.253.0'


def _sha(b):
    return hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()[:16]


def _read(name):
    """The file's LF text and whether it is CRLF on disk; refuses mixed endings and a file that is not the pinned one."""
    raw = (REPO / name).read_bytes()
    crlf, lf = raw.count(b"\r\n"), raw.count(b"\n")
    if crlf not in (0, lf):
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: deli_counter/%s has mixed line endings (%d CRLF of %d); nothing written"
                         % (name, crlf, lf))
    text = raw.decode("utf-8").replace("\r\n", "\n")
    if _sha(text.encode("utf-8")) != PINS[name]:
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: deli_counter/%s is %s, not the %s this patch was written against; nothing "
                         "written" % (name, _sha(text.encode("utf-8")), PINS[name]))
    return text, crlf > 0


def main(argv):
    # every file worked out and checked before any is written
    out = {}
    for name, edits in EDITS.items():
        text, crlf = _read(name)
        for what, old, new in edits:
            if text.count(old) != 1:
                raise SystemExit("REFUSED: deli_counter/%s: the anchor at %s is there %d times; nothing written"
                                 % (name, what, text.count(old)))
            text = text.replace(old, new)
        out[name] = text.replace("\n", "\r\n") if crlf else text
    # a refurnished spec is carried whole, the file it replaces pinned like any other
    for name, text in REPLACED.items():
        _old, crlf = _read(name)
        out[name] = text.replace("\n", "\r\n") if crlf else text
    for name in NEW_FILES:
        if (REPO / name).exists():
            raise SystemExit("REFUSED: deli_counter/%s exists already; nothing written" % name)
    v = REPO / "VERSION"
    if v.read_bytes().decode("utf-8") != OLD_VERSION:
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: VERSION reads %r, not %s; nothing written" % (v.read_text(), OLD_VERSION))
    cl = REPO / "CHANGELOG.md"
    craw = cl.read_bytes()
    if b"\r\n" in craw or not craw.startswith(b"## [" + OLD_VERSION.split()[-1].encode() + b"]"):
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: CHANGELOG.md is not LF opening on %s; nothing written" % OLD_VERSION)
    for name, text in out.items():
        (REPO / name).write_bytes(text.encode("utf-8"))
    for name, text in NEW_FILES.items():
        (REPO / name).write_bytes(text.encode("utf-8"))
    v.write_bytes(NEW_VERSION.encode("utf-8"))
    cl.write_bytes(CHANGELOG.encode("utf-8") + craw)
    print("%s applied: %d files edited, %d written, VERSION, CHANGELOG. Now, in deli_counter/: build.py --all, "
          "suite" % (NEW_VERSION, len(out), len(NEW_FILES)))
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
